    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Wer">Wer</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="392" ed="#liebermann"/>Twelfhyndes mannes wer is twelf hund scyllinga.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="392" ed="#liebermann"/>Twelfhyndes mannes wer is twelf hund scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="393" ed="#liebermann"/>Tƿelfhindi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Wer_1.lnote.oe.2"/> hominis weregildum est tƿelfhund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Wer_1.lnote.oe.3"/> scillinga (id est duodecies c solidi), qui faciunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Wer_1.lnote.oe.star2"/> libras uiginti quinque.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="393" ed="#liebermann"/>Wergeld eines 1200-Menschen ist 1200 Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Wer_1.lnote.de.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The wergild of a twelve-hundred man is 1200 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#wormald" corresp="#wit-h">A twelve-hundred man's wergeld is 1200 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator probably Wormald, The Making of English Law (named in the original spreadsheet’s sub-header rows): check; ‘qui faciunt libras uiginti quinque’ in the Quadripartitus is West Saxon reckoning (compare Af Rb. 31).</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Tuel. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Tuel. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hínd <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hínd MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Westsächsisch; vgl.</hi> Af. Rb. 31, <hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 19, <hi rend="italic">Sp.</hi> 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">West Saxon; cf. Af. Rb. 31, above p. 19, col. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wer_1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">231</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wergeld 9. Dieser Satz und 1, 1 umschreiben nur das Adjektiv <hi rend="italic">twelf(twi)hynde</hi> und klingen daher eher antiquarisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wergeld 9. This sentence and 1, 1 merely paraphrase the adjective <hi rend="italic">twelf(twi)hynde</hi> and therefore sound rather antiquarian</seg></note>
      </div>
